{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Better Late Than Never", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Simple Past vs Past Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'. <br /> You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished action that happened at a specific time in the past. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the <span class=\"underline\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had read up</span> on it before I moved to Boston.</span><br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? I read up on baseball.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I moved to Boston.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. <br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">Before I came to the States, I had only heard about how popular baseball was in Boston.</span><br /><br />  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about the action that happened after that prior action in the Past Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I had bought cheaper tickets at first, before you told me you liked sports.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had read up on it before I moved to Boston, but I didn't get very far in my research.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Possibility and Certainty ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.<br /> You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context.<br /> Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">must have heard</span> we all support the Red Sox here!</span><br /><br />   Must = it's very likely <br /> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br /> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br /> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Modal </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You must be familiar with home runs and innings.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely you are familiar with home runs and innings.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You couldn't possibly regret it!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not possible to regret it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Some games may be delayed or postponed because of that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible to delay the games.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "better late than never", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used when it's better for something to happen late than not at all", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Better late than never. You couldn't possibly regret it!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear and use when talking about baseball. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inning ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a division of a game during which the teams have the opportunity to score", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm sure you must be familiar with home runs and innings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hit it out of the park", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in baseball, to hit the ball hard enough to send it out of the field  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People had left right before our best player hit it out of the park.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to support", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be a fan of a team", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must have heard we all support the Red Sox here!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "incomprehensible ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "impossible to understand", "ty